def paste_as_link(run: Run, fixture: Path) -> None:
    """Copy a file, go somewhere else, `Ctrl+Alt+V` — and a link to it is there.

    `beta` already has an `inner.txt`, so the link is `inner.txt link`: the
    name it points at is tried first and refused by the create, which is the
    loop's whole mechanism. The free-name half is `edit`'s unit test, against
    real files. One `Ctrl+Z` takes the link away and leaves both files alone.
